      "v": "1. Loss to which sickness, disease, or myocardial infarction, including medical or surgical treatment thereof, is a contributing factor, except for any bacterial infection resulting from an accidental external cut or wound or accidental ingestion of contaminated food. 2. Caused by suicide, or intentionally self-inflicted injuries while sane. 3. Caused by or resulting from war or any act of war, declared or undeclared. 4. Caused by an accident that occurs while in the armed forces of any country - any premium paid for any period not covered while the Covered Person is in such service will be returned pro rata. 5. Caused by riot or insurrection. 6. Sustained during the Covered Person's commission or attempted commission of an assault or felony or engaging in any other illegal activity. 7. Sustained while piloting or serving as a crewmember or riding in any aircraft except as a fare-paying passenger on a regularly scheduled or charter airline. 8. Sustained while voluntarily taking drugs which federal law prohibits dispensing without a prescription, including sedatives, narcotics, barbiturates, amphetamines, or hallucinogens, unless the drug is taken as prescribed or administered by a licensed Physician. 9. Sustained as a result of the Insured being legally intoxicated from the use of alcohol; an Insured is conclusively determined to be legally intoxicated if a test administered in the jurisdiction where the Injury occurred is at or above the legal limit set by that jurisdiction. 10. Caused while riding in or on, entering into or alighting from, or being struck by a 2 or 3-wheeled motor vehicle or a motor vehicle not designed primarily for use on public streets and highways. 11. Caused by participation in or practice for interscholastic tackle football; intercollegiate sports; semi-professional sports; professional sports; ballooning, mountaineering, hang gliding, sky diving, parachuting, bungee jumping, spelunking, jet skiing, or scuba diving. 12. Caused by participation in or practice for motorized racing, speed test, or stunt show.",
      "vs": "VERIFIED_SINGLE_SOURCE"
    },
